note aemit: one alarm. A line in alarms.txt when it fires (name, value, threshold, source, key,
note volume in bytes); every alarm in alarms.json. Free-space alarms (6, 8) fire at or below
note their threshold, the others at or above it; reserve_refused (10) fires while the last reserve check
note refused a bring (until a later check finds room).
fn aemit i ulong v ulong th ulong json bool to void
fire = ge v th
if or eq i 6 eq i 8
fire = le v th
end
if eq i 10
fire = ne get aref 0 0
end
if json
if gt i 0
emb 44
end
emt kaj2
atext i false
emt kaj3
emn v
emt kaj4
emn th
emt kaj5
atext i true
emt kaj8
akey i true
emt kaj9
emn get avol i
emt kaj10
if fire
emt katrue
else
emt kafalse
end
emb 125
ret
end
if fire
atext i false
emb 9
emn v
emb 9
emn th
emb 9
atext i true
emb 9
akey i false
emb 9
emn get avol i
emb 10
end
end
