note ---- the reserves: the free bytes each filesystem keeps for the machine. The only refusal
note for room on intake. <work>reserve may set OPEN_RESERVE_STORAGE_BYTES (the filesystem of the
note Radicle storage and the work dir) and OPEN_RESERVE_DATA_BYTES (the filesystem of the open
note dir: spool, downloads), one NAME=digits line each; else the defaults below (measured, see
note docs/OPEN-BUILDS.md). A malformed line keeps the default.
fn rsvget which ulong to ulong
v = ulong 100000000000
if eq which 1
v = ulong 1073741824
end
wpath krsvf
fd = fopen pth 0 get pthl 0 557056 0
if lt fd 0
ret v
end
b = new uchar 512 0
k = read int fd b 0 512
x = fclose int fd
if le k 0
ret v
end
a = ulong 0
while lt a ulong k bound 512
e = a
while and lt e ulong k ne get b e 10 bound 512
e = add e 1
end
r = rsvline b a e which
if ge r 0
v = ulong r
end
a = add e 1
end
ret v
end
note rsvline: b[a, e) is the line NAME=digits for this which: its value, else -1
fn rsvline b view uchar 512 a ulong e ulong which ulong to long
n = len krsvs
if eq which 1
n = len krsvd
end
if le sub e a n
ret -1
end
for i ulong n bound 64
c = get krsvs i
if eq which 1
c = get krsvd i
end
if ne get b add a i c
ret -1
end
end
if gt sub sub e a n 19
ret -1
end
v = long 0
for i ulong sub sub e a n bound 19
c = get b add add a n i
if or lt c 48 gt c 57
ret -1
end
v = add mul v 10 long sub c 48
end
ret v
end
note rsvok: filesystem which keeps its reserve after need more bytes; else the refusal is
note recorded for the alarm (free bytes, need, the current did)
fn rsvok which ulong need ulong to bool
f = dfree which
r = rsvget which
if and ge f r ge sub f r need
put aref 0 0
ret true
end
arefuse which f need
ret false
end
